{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>He has broken</b> — He has destroyed. Likewise, <b>His hands shall complete</b> (Zechariah 4:9)."], :book :lamentations, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The lemma בצע in Lamentations 2:17 is rendered 'broken' in context; Ibn Ezra glosses it as כלה, 'completed/destroyed,' then cites the parallel use in Zechariah where the same root means 'complete.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Lamentations -- Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9C%D7%AA_%D7%90%D7%99%D7%9B%D7%94"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:07:35.071787218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}